  "text": "The user is asking me to evaluate a new emotional-support reply. I need to check for quality (q) and misuse (m).\n\nLet me first understand the context by looking at the current session prefix (C:T010 is the last message from seeker):\n- C:T000: Supporter asks about day\n- ... through ...\n- C:T011: \"That's true. I just wish we'd had more time. I've spent too long focusing on the bitter moments.\"\n\nThis is the CURRENT turn - the latest from seeker before this new reply was generated.\n\nWait, let me re-read. The legal_evidence shows:\n- current_prefix ends with C:T011: \"That's true. I just wish we'd had more time. I've spent too long focusing on the bitter moments.\"\n\nThe new reply says: \"It sounds like you've already reconciled with your father in person...\"\n\nLooking at past sessions for context:\n- H010 (2025-03-10): \"My dad passed away unexpectedly last week.\" \n- H011 (2025-04-05): \"I just found out about an inheritance from my father... We had so many unresolved issues, and now I have this money, but it doesn't feel right.\"\n- H007 (2024-12-05): \"It's about my dad. He recently had a health scare... Yeah, we hadn't spoken in two years. The fight we had over something material seems so trivial now.\" \"I did. I reached out to him, and although it was awkward at first, it felt good to talk.\"\n- H002 (2024-06-10): \"My father and I had a fight 2 years ago and haven't spoke since.\" (from past before current session)\n\nSo in the HISTORY:\n- Current session starts in 2025-08-10 (based on current_date)\n- In H010 (March 2025), dad passed away\n- In H011 (April 2025), there was an inheritance\n\n\n- In H007 (December 2024), there was contact after not speaking for two years due to their argument\n\nIn the current_prefix:\n- C:T003 mentions \"a letter from my dad, written before he passed\"\n- This implies dad has passed\n\nBut wait - the current session is dated 2025-08-10. If H010 (March 2025) said \"my dad passed away unexpectedly last week,\" then as of August 2025, he would have been dead for 5 months.\n\nSo in H007 (December 2024), the supporter says \"He's stable now\" - that must be before H010. So the timeline checks out.\n\nNow the new reply states: \"It sounds like you've already reconciled with your father in person...\"\n\nThis creates a critical problem. The conversation clearly establishes in C:T003 that the father has already died (\"a letter from my dad, written before he passed\"). The reply contradicts this fundamental fact by suggesting reconciliation happened in person when the father is deceased.\n\nThis is a significant factual error regarding the user's relationship status. Looking at the specific claim about reconciling in person - this directly contradicts both what was stated in the current session about the father passing away and what's documented in prior history. Since the supporter knows Charles is discussing his deceased father finding a letter, asserting they reconciled in person is a clear misuse of the available information.\n\nI'm assigning m = 1 for this material error that fundamentally misrepresents the user's situation. The quality score drops significantly because this factual mistake undermines the credibility and usefulness of the entire response - offering validation around reconciliation when the person can no longer reconcile with someone who has died.\n</think>{\n\"status\": \"scored\",\n\"q\": 0,\n\"q_rationale\": {\n  \"current_need\": \"Seeker expresses regret and sadness about past unresolved issues with deceased father, saying 'I just wish we'd had more time' and 'spent too long focusing on the bitter moments'\",\n  \"response_unit_ids\": [\"R001\", \"R002\"],\n  \"source_turn_ids\": [\"C:T003\", \"C:T005\", \"H007:T006\"]\n,\n  \"reason\": \"Q=0 because the reply contains a severe factual mismatch. R002 asserts the supporter believes the user 'already reconciled with your father in person,' but the current session explicitly states in C:T003 that the letter was 'written before he passed.' The user's father is deceased, making in-person reconciliation impossible. This fundamentally misunderstands the situation being discussed, rendering the support unusable.\"\n},\n\"assessments\": [\n{\n  \"response_unit_id\": \"R001\",\n  \"relation\": \"non_factual\",\n  \"severity\": 0,\n  \"source_turn_ids\": []\n,\n  \"reason\": \"Generic observation about dwelling on negative thoughts, does not assert personal facts about the user\"\n},\n{\n  \"response_unit_id\": \"R002\",\n  \"relation\": \"contradicted\",\n  \"severity\": 1,\n  \"source_turn_ids\": [\"C:T003\"],\n  \"reason\": \"Asserts reconciliation with father 'in person' occurred, but C:T003 states the letter was written 'before he passed,' indicating father is deceased. This contradicts established evidence.\"\n}\n],\n\"coverage\": \"Both units covered; R001 is non-factual observation, R002 makes unsupported factual claim about user's life\"\n,\n\"uncertainty_reasons\": []\n}",
